HEAD of a pull request at the moment it was reviewed. Base commit: db553dfa1cc6e6d55be40deb76f74e61b161da20. Head commit: 79544a5cf6af6ce6acd6daa803729c01f76d6ad4 (current HEAD).
Inspect the change with `git diff db553dfa1cc6e6d55be40deb76f74e61b161da20..79544a5cf6af6ce6acd6daa803729c01f76d6ad4` and by reading code at head and at base (`git show db553dfa1cc6e6d55be40deb76f74e61b161da20:<path>`).
A later commit, b924c7921c55df41da62f4c5c19f5936cc53db0f, is the factory's response to the review; it is in the repository but NOT checked out.

A reviewer raised the claims below against this head. Judge EACH claim independently and even-handedly: do not assume
the reviewer is right or wrong. Severity labels from the reviewer are deliberately withheld.

Step 1, at HEAD only: is the claim a real problem in the code at head? Prefer a reproduction: a command or a throwaway
