[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/integrations/lease-store.ts",
  "line": 114,
  "title": "Recovery: check that the tip is still `before` before accepting an equivalent record",
  "detail": "Recovery compares record equality before checking whether the tip is still `before` (~114-119). Journal a renewal whose fields equal the current record, then restart before sending it: recovery returns `applied`, although GitHub never received the renewal. Spec test 1 requires `dropped`, and #950 gives unchanged-tip detection precedence.\nCheck `before` first, then equivalence. Reproduced by the added regression below."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/integrations/lease-store.ts",
  "line": 132,
  "title": "Replay: classify a `moved` tip before calling the lease lost",
  "detail": "A replay marks ownership `lost` and clears the intent for every `moved` outcome (~132-134). Two cases reproduced:\n- Recovery reads the confirmed tip, then a delayed write with the same holder, run and generation lands before the replay's CAS. Recovery discards the final release/status/checkpoint, although no later generation superseded it.\n- A malformed intervening tip also becomes `lost` instead of staying uncertain.\nClassify `result.tip` with the recovery table first: same generation means retry or confirm, a later generation means lost, and an unreadable tip keeps the intent.\n\nRegressions (all fail at HEAD), to add to test/lease-store.test.ts:\n```ts\n\ntest(\"review regression: restart drops a renewal whose unchanged record was never sent\", async () => {\n  const f = fixture(true);\n  const before = f.confirmed();\n  f.journal(\"renew\", before, held);\n  f.reopen();\n  expect(await f.reconcile()).toBe(\"dropped\");\n  expect(f.store.leaseRow(repo, ref)).toMatchObject({\n    confirmed: { generation: 1, tip: before.sha, state: \"held\" },\n    intent: null,\n  });\n  expect(f.gh.calls(\"update\")).toHaveLength(0);\n});\n\ntest.each([\"same owner\", \"malformed\"])(\n  \"review regression: a replay moved to %s is not proof of supersession\",\n  async (mode) => {\n    const f = fixture();\n    const before = f.confirmed();\n    f.journal(\"release\", before);\n    f.gh.fault = (request) => {\n      if (request.step === \"update\")\n        f.gh.seed(mode === \"malformed\" ? \"invalid record\" : { ...held, status: \"waiting_input\" });\n    };\n    const result = await f.reconcile();\n    expect(f.store.leaseRow(repo, ref)?.confirmed).toEqual({\n      generation: 1,\n      tip: before.sha,\n      state: \"held\",\n    });\n    expect(f.store.leaseRow(repo, ref)?.intent).toMatchObject({ op: \"release\", record: release });\n    expect(result).toBe(\"pending\");\n  },\n);\n\n```"
 }
]
